they considered to be lords? C20 (page 62) explains that all lords of Households hold title of minimum Knight and are almost all at least a Baron. When Seif was ennobled, he became a knight. Does this mean any kith could become attain the rank of Squire/Esquire even before the Shattering (if, albeit, under extreme difficulty)?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If we can compare them to real world nobility, Squires are people who were being groomed to become members of the nobility. After a training period of roughly 10 years, they would be granted Knighthood, which was the lowest rank of nobility back in those days.<br /> <br /> So simply put, a Squire is not technically a noble at the time, but they will eventually become one after a suitable period of service.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}